# 1. Concept: Motion from Bounding Boxes

Each track already has a history like:

```json
[
 {"frame":650,"bbox":[430,360,560,470]},
 {"frame":655,"bbox":[435,360,565,470]},
 {"frame":660,"bbox":[440,360,570,470]}
]
```

From this we compute the **center of the bounding box**.

```text
center_x = (x1 + x2) / 2
center_y = (y1 + y2) / 2
```

This gives the **object position in pixels**.

---

# 2. Compute Pixel Displacement

Example:

```text
frame 650 → center (495,415)
frame 660 → center (505,415)
```

Movement:

```text
dx = 10 pixels
dy = 0
distance ≈ 10 pixels
```

---

# 3. Convert to Speed

Speed formula:

```text
speed = distance / time
```

Time difference:

```text
Δt = frame_difference / fps
```

Example:

```text
10 pixels / 0.5 seconds
```

This gives **pixels per second**.

Later we can convert to **km/h using camera calibration**.

